    {
      "text": "Whisk vinegar, soy sauce, olive oil, parsley, basil, oregano, garlic powder, and black pepper together in a bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/OcruVMtPWVXxN13kg-PkyX9TH8s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/241890-grilled-chicken-marinade-step2-245-1-84ca06e6c4664c98b8c68c76917461e6.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/241890/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour into a resealable plastic bag. Add chicken, coat with the marinade, squeeze out excess air, and seal the bag. Marinate in the refrigerator, 2 to 4 hours.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/T0aA2nAg2-Fvt1syNqxTLPqQi0o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/241890-grilled-chicken-marinade-step3-248-1-b846ee3f786b475193555f9098b5aea3.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/241890/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat grill for medium-low heat and lightly oil the grate. Drain and discard marinade.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Grill chicken on the preheated grill until no longer pink in the center, 4 to 5 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
